request.description:
This endpoint only creates product data; prices are set afterwards through the price-plan endpoints. `status`, when sent, must be `draft` (any other value: 422 `in`). Draft requires only the name; without `sku` a free one is generated (`SKU-` + 8 hex characters). A Draft does not hold its SKU: several Drafts may share one, but a SKU claimed by a product that has left Draft → 422 `sku_taken`. The SKU is claimed when the product leaves Draft (changeProductStatus).
Admin "save" flow for one form (the FE runs the calls in order):
1. `POST /admin/products` → product in Draft;
2. `POST /admin/products/{product}/price-plans` → Default price (for a configurable: one plan per variant, or `POST /admin/price-plans/bulk`);
3. `POST /admin/products/{product}/status` → `active` (rejected with 422 until every sellable product has a Default price).

With `variants` (configurable only) at most 100 variants are created in this call; larger sets → 422 `too_many_combinations` (create the product, then use variants/generate). Variant SKUs not sent are generated as in generateProductVariants; simulateProductVariants shows them before saving. Errors of the variant step carry the generateProductVariants field names under `variants.` (e.g. `variants.combinations.{i}.sku` → `sku_taken`, `sku_duplicate`, `sku_invalid`), all in the same 422.

